WEBVTT

00:00:00.556 --> 00:00:02.386
Two ways to lock a message.

00:00:02.891 --> 00:00:05.301
Same key for both, or a key pair.

00:00:05.826 --> 00:00:07.036
Each has a job.

00:00:08.789 --> 00:00:10.379
Symmetric cryptography.

00:00:11.089 --> 00:00:14.319
One secret key for
encryption and decryption.

00:00:14.859 --> 00:00:17.289
Fast, so it is used for bulk data.

00:00:17.819 --> 00:00:20.269
But the key must be shared safely first.

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:23.652
Asymmetric cryptography.

00:00:24.472 --> 00:00:28.362
A public key and a private key,
mathematically related.

00:00:28.912 --> 00:00:32.062
Public encrypts,
private decrypts for confidentiality.

00:00:33.117 --> 00:00:33.987
Private signs,

00:00:34.497 --> 00:00:38.387
public verifies for authentication
and non-repudiation.

00:00:40.089 --> 00:00:41.359
Symmetric is fast.

00:00:42.079 --> 00:00:43.529
Asymmetric is slower.

00:00:44.224 --> 00:00:49.594
So asymmetric distributes keys and signs;
symmetric encrypts the data.

00:00:51.256 --> 00:00:52.406
Symmetric examples:

00:00:52.976 --> 00:00:54.296
DES, AES,

00:00:54.736 --> 00:00:58.566
Blowfish, RC5, IDEA, RC4.

00:00:59.051 --> 00:01:00.341
Asymmetric examples:

00:01:01.011 --> 00:01:04.041
RSA, ElGamal, knapsack, Diffie-Hellman.

00:01:04.576 --> 00:01:06.846
Diffie-Hellman is key exchange only.

00:01:08.522 --> 00:01:10.132
One key or a key pair.

00:01:10.662 --> 00:01:13.732
Fast bulk data, or safe key distribution.

00:01:14.347 --> 00:01:16.217
Modern systems use both.

